{"classified_as":[{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300078925","label":"watercolors (paintings)","type":"Type"},{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/object/8334","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"catalogue raisonnée number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026061"}],"content":"184","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":"184, Catalogue Raisonné","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"8334","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Nude Series V","type":"Name"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":{"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Whitney Archive.","title":"Seated Nude","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"notes":"Source of title: Downtown Gallery Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks.","title":"Nude No. V","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: backing inscription 1.","title":"Nude Series V","type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}},"type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe","id":"actor/2","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_post_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_post_1999"}],"content":["Though widely dated to 1917, PMA dates this work to 1918. The 1917 date is supported by a label on the frame in O'Keeffe's hand, and is published in the catalogue raisonné (Lynes, 1999, no. 184) and elsewhere. However, some scholarship suggests that *Nude Series V* was made in 1918, after O'Keeffe recovered from illness during the winter of 1917‑1918, and when letters between O'Keeffe, Paul Strand, and Alfred Stieglitz record O'Keeffe painting Leah Harris, a possible model for the Nude Series watercolors. Shoemaker, Innis H., *Adventures in Modern Art: the Charles K. Williams II Collection*. Philadelphia: Philadelphia Museum of Art, 2009, 227‑8 includes the following references;see full entry for more detail: Roxana Robinson, *Georgia O'Keeffe: A Life* (New York: Harper \u0026 Rowe, 1989), p. 199 and p. 580, note 50 seems to have been the first to suggest that the watercolors depict Leah Harris and that they probably date from early 1918. The complicated story of the relationship of O'Keeffe, Harris, and Strand in the spring of 1918 is recounted in Benita Eisler, *O''Keeffe and Stieglitz: An American Romance* (New York: Penguin Books, 1991), pp. 167‑179. Strands' letter to Stieglitz is quoted on p. 177. Eisler suggests that the nudes were made in two campaigns, beginning in late 1917, but all evidence points to the fact that because of her ill health O'Keeffe was not working between November 1917 and February 1918. Labels inscribed in O'Keeffe' own hand on two of the watercolors, including *Nude Series V*, indicate a date of 1917. However, Lynes, Vol. 1, p. 19 notes that O'Keeffe often wrote the wrong date on the backs of her pictures. (Source: Philadelphia Museum of Art, 2025)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. Nude Series V, 1917. Watercolor on wove paper, 11 15/16 x 8 7/8 inches. Philadelphia Museum of Art. Gift of C. K. Williams, II, 2019. © Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Philadelphia Museum of Art","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Watercolor on wove paper","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Flowing, loosely rendered brushstrokes come together to produce the form of a nude person. The figure is seated, and their left side glows pale purple due to an unseen light source. The rest of their body has been rendered in shades of dark red, blue, and purple. The figure contrasts with the exposed white paper that constitutes the work's background.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"Nude Series V, 1917","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"11 15/16 x 8 7/8 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Gift of C. K. Williams, II, 2019","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Whitney Archive indicates, \"Exam. at Whitney Mus. May 1946. . . .Probably painted 1915 or 1916.\" Whitney Archive dates 1915/1916. Downtown Gallery Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks date 1917. Pictured in 1923 New York (Anderson) Stieglitz installation photograph, see Appendix III, figure 21. See cat. no. 176. (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Watercolor on wove paper, 11 15/16 x 8 7/8 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"extended_medium_description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/extended_medium_description"}],"content":"Watercolor on moderately thick, cream, smooth wove paper with a slightly fuzzy feel\n(Source: Paper Survey researched by Judith C. Walsh and published in Lynes, 1999.)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"Estate of the artist; private collection, 1986‑94; with Marissa G. Boyescu Arts, Miami, by 1994; sold to C. K. Williams, II, Philadelphia, October 29, 1994; gift to PMA, 2019. \n(Source: Philadelphia Museum of Art, 2025)","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/857719/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digitally_available_via":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/857719"}],"conforms_to":[{"id":"http://iiif.io/api/image","type":"InformationObject"}],"format":"application/ld+json;profile='http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json'","type":"DigitalService"}],"type":"DigitalObject"}],"type":"VisualItem"}],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}